name: hub-session-start
description: Start a work session against the unified-agent hub by confirming identity, reading broadcasts and the task queue, and claiming one task before changing code. Use at the start of a session in this project or when asked what to work on next.
---

# Hub session start

1. Call `profile_status()`. If the hub is unreachable or the identity is
   empty, report that and stop. Do not work unregistered.
2. Call `memory_search("broadcast", tags=["broadcast"])` and read every
   current broadcast before choosing work.
3. Call `task_list(status="doing")`, then `task_list(status="open")`. Prefer
   high-priority rows, but read past them.
4. Claim exactly one task: `task_claim(id, agent="<your label>")`. If another
   agent holds it, choose a different task.
5. Work in the task's own worktree or branch. When you finish, record the pull
   request with `task_update(id, evidence_ref="<PR URL>")` and stop. Merging
   follows the rules in `AGENTS.md`.
